Summary of all changes for M6 remaining audio wiring
=====================================================

=== 1. AudioBackend.h — Add setReverbVolume to the interface ===
Added: virtual void setReverbVolume(const std::string& reverbName, float volume)
       to AudioBackend, defaulting to no-op.

=== 2. AxmolAudioBackend.h — Implement setReverbVolume + reverb stub ===
Added: - _reverbVolumes map field
       - setReverbVolume() override that stores the volume
       - update() override that stubs future axmol reverb API integration

=== 3. AudioManager.cpp — Compute reverb volume each frame ===
Changed update() to compute cathedral reverb volume from activeLayer and
underground (matching web audioManager.ts lines 176-181), then call
_backend->setReverbVolume("cathedral", reverbVolume).
Moved sameAudioLayer to MathUtil.h so other modules can use it.

=== 4. MathUtil.h — Add sameAudioLayer ===
Added: inline bool math::sameAudioLayer(int a, int b) for use by Barns.cpp.

=== 5. Barns.h — Add bullet sound fields to BulletVisual ===
Added: uint16_t playerId, bool whizHeard to BulletVisual.

=== 6. Barns.cpp — Wire explosion per-def sounds, bullet whiz, shot sounds ===

BulletBarn::spawn: Copy playerId + reset whizHeard.

BulletBarn::update: On each frame, check if the bullet is close to the camera
(<7.5 units), same audio layer, not from active player → play bullet_whiz
group once (port of bullet.ts lines 221-233).

ShotBarn::update: On shot.ticker==0, play weapon shoot sound with:
- Base sound name = weaponType + "_01" (soundDefs convention)
- Channel = activePlayer or otherPlayers based on playerId
- Detune for trailSaturated (+300) and splinter (-300)
- Secondary layers for splinter (+1200, delay 30ms, vol 0.75)
- AP rounds (+1000, delay 45ms, vol 0.75)
- High velocity (+800, delay 10ms, vol 2.0, no muffled filter)
(Port of shot.ts lines 114-200.)

GameWorld.cpp: Replace generic "explosion_01" with per-type sound map
containing all 20 explosion effect types with grass/water sound names,
detune, and volume. Stub surface lookup via Map::getGroundSurface.
(Port of explosion.ts lines 193-215 + ExplosionEffectDefs map.)

=== 7. M6_AUDIO.md — Update remaining/not ported section ===
Added status of each item, noting what's wired and what's still out of scope.

=== What is deliberately NOT wired (out of scope or M7) ===
- Player footstep surface groups (Player has no surface/stepDistance state)
- Player bush enter/exit, door error, weapon deploy/switch, heal/reload/pickup sounds
- Player haste effect, dry fire, bleeding sounds
- UI sounds (no UI system in the C++ port yet)
- Full axmol reverb convolution (setReverbProperties not called; volume stored)
- Volume/persisted settings UI (M7)